```julia
p1 = plot(t_grid, [u[6] for u in exact_ref.u], title = "U₁ (node 1 potential)",
          xlabel = "t [s]", ylabel = "V", legend = false)
p2 = plot(t_grid, [u[7] for u in exact_ref.u], title = "U₂ (node 2 potential)",
          xlabel = "t [s]", ylabel = "V", legend = false)
p3 = plot(t_grid, [u[8] for u in exact_ref.u], title = "U₃ (node 3 potential)",
          xlabel = "t [s]", ylabel = "V", legend = false)
p4 = plot(t_grid, [u[9] for u in exact_ref.u], title = "I (current)",
          xlabel = "t [s]", ylabel = "A", legend = false)
plot(p1, p2, p3, p4, layout = (2, 2), size = (800, 600),
     plot_title = "Charge Pump — Exact Solution")
```

```julia
plot(t_grid, [u[1] for u in exact_ref.u],
     title = "Y_T1 (gate charge)",
     xlabel = "t [s]", ylabel = "C", legend = false)
```

## Omissions

This is one of the hardest problems in the IVP Test Set. The following solver classes
are **not** included in the WPD because they fail on this index-2 system:

- **Mass-matrix ODE solvers** (Rodas4, Rodas5P, FBDF, QNDF, RadauIIA5): all return `Unstable`
- **DASSL.dassl()**: returns without progressing (2 steps, initial conditions unchanged)
- **DFBDF**: returns `Unstable`
- **IDA without `tstops`**: returns `MaxIters` (cannot pass the first discontinuity at $t = 50\,\text{ns}$)
- **DASKR at tolerances below $10^{-3}$**: `ConvergenceFailure`
- **IDA at tolerances of $10^{-4}$ and below**: `Unstable` at $t \approx 1.2 \times 10^{-7}$
  ($10^{-4}$) or `ConvergenceFailure` at $t \approx 5.01 \times 10^{-8}$ ($10^{-5}$ to
  $10^{-8}$), both at points where the transistor switches operating region

## Work-Precision Benchmarks

Only the DAE residual form is benchmarked, with IDA and DASKR both run at tolerances
$10^{-1}$ to $10^{-3}$. Errors are measured against the exact solution. A run that does not
reach $t_{end}$ has no error value and is left out of the diagrams, so the return codes at
each tolerance are printed first.

```julia
for tol in 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (1:3),
    (name, alg, save_everystep) in [("IDA", IDA(), false), ("DASKR", DASKR.daskr(), false),
                                    ("DASKR, save_everystep = true", DASKR.daskr(), true)]
    sol = solve(daeprob, alg; abstol = tol, reltol = tol, save_everystep,
                maxiters = Int(1e5), dt = 1e-15, tstops = disc_times)
    println(rpad(name, 29), " tol = $tol: retcode = $(sol.retcode), t_final = $(sol.t[end]), ",
            "saved points = $(length(sol.t)), final error in y[9] = $(abs(sol.u[end][9] - u_end[9]))")
end
```

IDA completes every tolerance. DASKR does not produce a single point in the final-value
diagram:

- At $10^{-1}$, DASKR stops with `ConvergenceFailure` at $t \approx 1.01 \times 10^{-6}$
  (`ABS(H)=HMIN`). It fails there with `save_everystep = true` as well, so this is a genuine
  solver failure at that tolerance.
- At $10^{-2}$ and $10^{-3}$, DASKR returns `MaxIters` with only the initial point saved. With
  `save_everystep = false`, each DDASKR call integrates to $t_{end}$, and DDASKR returns after 500
  internal steps expecting to be called again. The DASKR.jl wrapper (v3.2.0) treats that return
  as final. With `save_everystep = true`, the same solves reach $t_{end}$. The timeseries diagram
  below saves every step, so it contains these two DASKR points.

### Loose Tolerances (Final-Value Error)

```julia
abstols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (1:3)
reltols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (1:3)

setups = [
    Dict(:prob_choice => 1, :alg => IDA()),
    Dict(:prob_choice => 1, :alg => DASKR.daskr()),
]

wp = WorkPrecisionSet(probs, abstols, reltols, setups;
    save_everystep = false, appxsol = refs, maxiters = Int(1e5), numruns = 1,
    names = ["IDA", "DASKR"], dt = 1e-15, tstops = disc_times)
plot(wp, title = "Charge Pump DAE — Loose Tolerances (Final Value)")
```

### Loose Tolerances (L₂ Timeseries Error)

The timeseries error is computed at every step the solver saves, so this diagram saves every
step.

```julia
abstols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (1:3)
reltols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (1:3)

setups = [
    Dict(:prob_choice => 1, :alg => IDA()),
    Dict(:prob_choice => 1, :alg => DASKR.daskr()),
]

wp = WorkPrecisionSet(probs, abstols, reltols, setups; error_estimate = :l2,
    appxsol = refs, maxiters = Int(1e5), numruns = 1,
    names = ["IDA", "DASKR"], dt = 1e-15, tstops = disc_times)
plot(wp, title = "Charge Pump DAE — Loose Tolerances (L₂ Timeseries)")
```

### Conclusion

Against the exact solution, IDA's final-value error drops from about $2 \times 10^{-2}$ at
tolerances $10^{-1}$ and $10^{-2}$ to below $10^{-6}$ at $10^{-3}$. DASKR fails at $10^{-1}$
and, with `save_everystep = false`, stops at the first 500-step return at $10^{-2}$ and
$10^{-3}$. In the timeseries diagram, where every step is saved, DASKR reaches $t_{end}$ at
$10^{-2}$ and $10^{-3}$, with smaller errors than IDA at the same tolerances and longer run
times.

